{
  "family": "bold",
  "familyName": "Bold",
  "summary": "Confident and loud: oversized type, wide fields of strong colour and big rounded shapes.",
  "principles": [
    "Headlines are huge and tight; the page has one dominant thing.",
    "Whole sections in the primary or accent colour, not just buttons.",
    "Big soft corners and generous padding.",
    "High contrast everywhere; colour carries emphasis, not decoration."
  ],
  "componentNotes": [
    "Headings: the heading face at display sizes, very tight tracking; key numbers just as big.",
    "Sections: alternate plain sections with full-width bands in the primary colour (text in its foreground) or the accent.",
    "Buttons: pill-shaped, solid, large; secondary buttons outlined in the text colour.",
    "Cards and tiles: 16px corners, soft deep shadows, often filled with a tint of the primary.",
    "Labels: small, uppercase and wide-spaced, set against the big type."
  ],
  "personality": "- Components (the kit draws them this way; use the ds-* classes and never restyle them): corners soft, depth raised, spacing balanced, type dramatic; buttons solid, cards filled, inputs filled, navigation filled, tables zebra, icons bold.\n- Colour amount 3 of 4: colour on bands and feature panels too.\n- Voice: Confident and punchy: short headlines that make a claim, then get out of the way. Write every label, heading, empty state and message this way.",
